          "path": "_m/d/n/r/u/silent-sam-wp/postcard-photograph-un.jpg",
          "filename": "Silent Sam unveiling, Postcard, 1913.jpg",
          "caption": "A postcard photograph of the unveiling of the Confederate Monument Silent Sam at the University of North Carolina on June 2, 1913. \nThe postcard was sent by \"Drew\", on the very day of the unveiling, to Mrs. M.F. Patterson in Winston-Salem, N.C., and says: \"My dear Mother, This is a photo. of the unveiling of our new monument to those who left the Univ. to enlist in the army in 1861. The parade yesterday was a fine one, &amp; Mary &amp; the other looked very picturesque in your dresses. We'll take good care of them &amp; thank you for them. All well. Love to all. Affectionately, Drew.\" .",
          "alt": "A postcard photograph of the unveiling of the Confederate Monument Silent Sam at the University of North Carolina on June 2, 1913. \nThe postcard was sent by \"Drew\", on the very day of the unveiling, to Mrs. M.F. Patterson in Winston-Salem, N.C., and says: \"My dear Mother, This is a photo. of the unveiling of our new monument to those who left the Univ. to enlist in the army in 1861. The parade yesterday was a fine one, &amp; Mary &amp; the other looked very picturesque in your dresses. We'll take good care of them &amp; thank you for them. All well. Love to all. Affectionately, Drew.\" .",
          "width": 1200,
          "height": 765,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "Unknown author",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silent_Sam_unveiling,_Postcard,_1913.jpg",
